# Robustness of the landmarks and measurement

It is not know that how good the quality of the images need to be to establish a set of effective measurements. I will compare the measurements from a "good quanlity " images and "bad quality" images (when animals are moving, contracting, twisting, or not up right to the camera) at two different scope and quantify the robustness of the landmark and measreuments.

I took 3 FL animals from different stages with different sizes (from 202509 diff temp experiments 16C group) and imaged their OA, PA, TA planes on 2 scopes using 2 cameras. Each plane has 10 images.

## Measurements from good quality image
The measurements from good quality images are generated by measuring a same good image 10 times. (for L, T, C)

PA:1-PA.tif, 2-PA-12.tif, 3-PA-11.tif
TA: 1-TA-2.tif, 
OA: 1-OA.tif, 2-OA-9.tif, 3-OA-6.tif

